Use the ANT build.xml file to get a working custom GUI.

Relevant for using AJAX in your GUI:

rcms.fm.ajaxFM.MyFunctionManager:
	contains the logic for GUI commands
	also starts and stops the ChangedParameterSender

rcms.fm.ajaxFM.MyParameterSet:
	a custom ParameterSet class that provides methods for taking snapshots and comparing parameter sets
	this allows to only send changed parameters and accumulate parameter updates
	
rcms.fm.ajaxFM.notificationsToGUI.parameters.ChangedParameterSender:
	this class runs in its own thread and periodically sends changed parameters to the GUI using the notification system
	
rcms.fm.ajaxFM.updatesFromGUI.MySetParameterHandler:
	this handler processes parameter set events and processes GUI commands
	 it also needs to inform the ChangedParameterSender about changes to GUI-relevant parameters
	 
js/

	ajaxRequest.js:
		the AJAXRequest library
		
	ajaxRequestFunctions.js:
		simple functions to update FM parameters using the AJAXRequest library
		
	GUI.js:
		a small JS class that provides functions to update FM parameters using jQuery
		
	jquery-*.min.js:
		the jQuery library
		
	notifications.js:
		processes incoming notifications and is responsible for updating the document to reflect parameter changes
		
jsp/controlPanel.jsp:
	the main JSP that outputs HTML and JS that is capable of sending parameter updates and commands using AJAX
	and receives and processes parameter updates from the notification system
	
general notes:
	"return false;" is used after most JS functions on form elements. For buttons and button inputs,
		this prevents some browsers from sending the form the used element belongs to.
	For AJAX-only inputs, it is recommended that you always add "return false;" after the function call,
		just to make sure the page is not reloaded when they are being used.